              <div class="text-sm font-bold text-white mb-1">Four Discrete Clusters in Under 2 Seconds</div>
              <p class="text-xs text-neutral-400 leading-relaxed font-normal">
                Because physical exposure parameters differ drastically between calibration sets, you never need to guess which black thumbnail is which. The clusters separate cleanly on the graph.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <h2 class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-bold text-white mt-12 mb-4 tracking-tight flex items-center gap-3">
            <span class="h-6 w-1 rounded-full bg-[#00FFFF]"></span>
            <span>Step-by-Step Workflow with AstroPlot RAW</span>
          </h2>

          <p>
            We built <a href="/software/astroplot" class="text-[#00FFFF] underline hover:text-white transition-colors">AstroPlot RAW</a> to make this process instantaneous. It reads raw EXIF metadata directly in parallel across all CPU cores without full debayering:
          </p>

          <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-white mt-8 mb-3">1. Drop Your SD Card Folder</h3>
          <p>
            Drag and drop your raw shoot directory directly onto AstroPlot RAW. The app parses 500+ RAW files in 2 to 3 seconds and plots them on the canvas.
          </p>

          <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-white mt-8 mb-3">2. Marquee-Select &amp; Tag Each Cluster</h3>
          <p>
            Click and drag a box over each cluster, then press the hotkey to assign the category:
          </p>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2">
            <li>Press <strong class="text-white">L</strong> to tag as <code class="font-mono text-xs bg-black/40 text-[#00FFFF] px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">Lights</code></li>
            <li>Press <strong class="text-white">D</strong> to tag as <code class="font-mono text-xs bg-black/40 text-[#00FFFF] px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">Darks</code></li>
            <li>Press <strong class="text-white">F</strong> to tag as <code class="font-mono text-xs bg-black/40 text-[#00FFFF] px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">Flats</code></li>
            <li>Press <strong class="text-white">B</strong> to tag as <code class="font-mono text-xs bg-black/40 text-[#00FFFF] px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">Biases</code></li>
          </ul>

          <!-- GIF Demo Card -->
          <div class="rounded-2xl border border-white/10 bg-[#101726] overflow-hidden my-8 shadow-2xl">
            <img src="/software/astroplot/blog/how-to-pre-sort-raw-files-for-siril/astroplotraw2.gif" alt="Marquee selecting and tagging raw photo clusters in AstroPlot RAW" class="w-full h-auto block" loading="lazy" />
            <div class="p-4 sm:p-5 border-t border-white/10 bg-[#0c121e]">
              <span class="font-mono text-xs font-semibold text-[#00FFFF] uppercase tracking-wider block mb-1">Fast Hotkey Tagging</span>
              <div class="text-sm font-bold text-white mb-1">Tag Hundreds of Files in Seconds</div>
              <p class="text-xs text-neutral-400 leading-relaxed font-normal">
                Marquee select any cluster with your mouse and tap L, D, F, or B. Colors change instantly to confirm assignment.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-white mt-8 mb-3">3. Click "Organize"</h3>
          <p>
            Choose whether to <strong class="text-white">Copy</strong> or <strong class="text-white">Move</strong> files, select your target working folder, and click Organize. AstroPlot RAW automatically generates the standard Siril subdirectories and places every file into its proper location.
          </p>
          <div class="rounded-xl border border-[#00FFFF]/30 bg-[#00FFFF]/5 p-4 my-6 text-sm text-neutral-200">
            <strong class="text-[#00FFFF]">Safe by Design:</strong> Every operation is tracked in a local SQLite transaction log. If you ever make a mistake, simply click <strong class="text-white">"Undo Last Move"</strong> to return 100% of your files to their exact original locations.
          </div>

          <h2 class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-bold text-white mt-12 mb-4 tracking-tight flex items-center gap-3">
            <span class="h-6 w-1 rounded-full bg-[#00FFFF]"></span>
            <span>Running Siril's OSC_Preprocessing Script</span>
          </h2>

          <p>
            Now that your files are neatly organized in under 60 seconds, launching your stack in Siril takes just four clicks:
          </p>
          <ol class="list-decimal pl-6 space-y-2">
            <li>Open <strong class="text-white">Siril</strong>.</li>
            <li>Click the <strong class="text-white">Home</strong> icon at the top toolbar and set your working directory to the folder created by AstroPlot RAW.</li>
            <li>Click <strong class="text-white">Scripts &rarr; OSC_Preprocessing</strong> (or <strong class="text-white">OSC_Preprocessing_WithoutFlat</strong> if you didn't shoot flats).</li>
            <li>Walk away and go to sleep. Siril will build your master darks, master biases, master flats, debayer, register, normalize, and produce your final stacked <code class="font-mono text-xs bg-black/40 text-[#00FFFF] px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">result.fit</code> completely unattended.</li>
          </ol>
        </div>

